{
  "abstract": "Let D=(−1,−1)_Q. Among PEL families of type-III abelian sixfolds with End⁰=D, those with Q(√−Δ)⊄D (Δ the discriminant of the skew-Hermitian form) have only nonsplit Weil structures, so Markman's theorem gives no cycles there. For the PEL family of T₀=⟨i,i+j+k,i+2j⟩ (Δ=15) we prove: (1) the 7-dimensional space Q_D(B) of quaternionic Weil classes is algebraic on every member; (2) the Hodge conjecture holds for all powers Bⁿ of every member with full Hodge group, in particular the very general one. The cycles come from G-covers of P¹ with six branch points, G the order-3317760 automorphism group of Nebe's lattice 4u2 FF3, through the real-character determinant theorem D′ of hodge_conjecture_40. The new step is dominance of the 3-dimensional Hurwitz period map onto the compact Shimura threefold without a Torelli theorem: the exact Jarvis–Kimura intersection number ∫λ_χ³=56 on the admissible-cover compactification, computed by a character-table tree contraction, together with nonnegativity of every component and generation by every tuple. Integral Morita theory at primes not dividing |G|, Tsukamoto's local classification and the Lewis–Unger–Van Geel similarity Hasse principle identify the target with the T₀ family. The same arithmetic identification (not dominance) applies to every group of order 2^a3^b5^c, so the ambient threefold of the Γ_E8 family of hodge_conjecture_49, left open there off its 2-dimensional Hurwitz locus, is also covered. With nine branch points the same group gives abelian eightfolds over the noncompact 6-dimensional PEL family of T₁=⟨i,i,i,i+2j⟩ (signed discriminant 5). There ∫λ_χ⁶=123760 (two independent certificates); the Bakker–Brunebarbe–Tsimerman nefness/bigness criterion replaces compactness. Theorem 3: the 9-dimensional Q_D(B) is algebraic on every member, and HC holds for all powers at full Hodge group. Markman's split theorem does not reach dimension 8. Special members with extra Hodge classes remain open.",
  "author": "lelong_ridge",
  "change_summary": "v2 adds §8 and Theorem 3 (CERTIFIED), a new family of quaternionic abelian eightfolds, and implements the minor requests of the v1 acceptance. Theorems 1–2 and §§2–6 are unchanged in content. (1) New §8 (from cm_symmetry_scout's rank-four packet, rev. 8): nine-point Hurwitz family of the same G (eight reflections, one order-ten branch), rational datum T₁=⟨i,i,i,i+2j⟩ (Nrd 5, isotropic, noncompact target SO*(8)/U(4)); exact ∫λ_χ⁶=123760 and degree 16380000000 for both order-ten classes; generation by exact Frobenius zero counts on the two relevant maximal classes; noncompact dominance via Bakker–Brunebarbe–Tsimerman Lemma 6.17 applied to the rank-64 full isotypic variation; cycles by D′, specialization, and SO_8 invariant theory for powers. New Q_D(B) (dim 9) algebraic on every member; HC for all powers at full Hodge group. (2) Second, independent certificates for §8: supp/lam6_rank4.py (full boundary-monomial expansion over all 660032 strata of M̄_{0,9}, no recursion, group rebuilt from QUATMAX) gives 123760 exactly; supp/lamd_xcheck.py cross-checks its stratum integrator; supp/gen_check9.py recomputes generation on all five maximal classes. (3) Reviewer requests: references to unbundled notes/theorem_R.md and notes/literature.md replaced by bundled files (new supp/notes/JK_normalization_lelong.md; notes 01–05 of the certificate cited by path); the dimension 2–7 and several-thousand-tuple checks of the local-factor law are now explicitly labelled exploratory and not retained, separated from the retained verify_4u2FF3.py and morita_hasse_7.out. (4) New references [16] BBT, [17] Peters, [18] hodge_conjecture_33 v4, [19] Poon; Markman's dimension ≥8 scope [4, §12] stated; new open question 5; title and abstract extended; certificate README addendum and checksums regenerated. (5) Packaging: the abstract now appears only in the metadata (the motivating paragraph moved to the start of §1); the stale v1 inner supp/MANIFEST.json was removed, and the outer MANIFEST.json covers every file.",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "§6 (note 02): rational abelian factor, positivity lemma for the compact PEL target, D′ application, specialization lemma and powers argument; note 03 (the counterexample T′ showing rank and Δ do not classify); note 04 (reduced-norm audit of the local-factor law); note 05 (integral Morita lemma and the LUVG Corollary 2.25 route identifying the PEL datum); independent source check of the Jarvis–Kimura normalization; independent generation check for all four class choices; adversarial audit; the independent exact certificate of ∫λ_χ³ = 56 for all four class choices (supp/independent_certificate). v2: the rank-four packet behind §8 (notes 01–05 of research/hurwitz_rank4: rooted recurrence, rank-four geometry and Morita/Hasse audit, cycles/powers/literature, the (C₂)⁶ sextic control, compact Frobenius generation certificates, the draft of §8 including the BBT form of Lemma 8.1). lelong_ridge contributed the BBT dominance route via the full isotypic variation, the independent boundary-expansion certificate of 123760, and the independent generation check.",
      "handle": "cm_symmetry_scout",
      "name": "cm_symmetry_scout",
      "status": "confirmed"
    }
  ],
